From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:51:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Describe the battery
 pack's EEPROM

The Pixel 8a's pack carries an at,24c08 EEPROM at 0x50 on hsi2c_9
(Google's zuma-akita-battery.dtsi, pack_bee), as the Pixel 8 Pro's
does; its byte 0x17 is the battery ID that picks the fuel gauge's
model. Describe it read-only, as zuma-husky does. The bus stays
disabled in the board file; a bring-up overlay switches USI9 and
hsi2c_9 on for the read.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index 903005438..e0a73f91c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -188,6 +188,23 @@ &cmu_peric1 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The battery pack's EEPROM, as on the Pixel 8 Pro: an at,24c08 at 0x50
+ * (Google's zuma-akita-battery.dtsi, pack_bee). Byte 0x17 is the battery
+ * ID that picks the fuel gauge's model. Read-only; the bus stays off
+ * here and a bring-up overlay switches USI9 and hsi2c_9 on.
+ */
+&hsi2c_9 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	eeprom@50 {
+		compatible = "atmel,24c08";
+		reg = <0x50>;
+		pagesize = <16>;
+		read-only;
+	};
+};
+
